      "label": "No vulnerability there",
      "entryType": 1,
      "author": "matus-pintek",
      "details": {
        "severity": "Informational",
        "difficulty": "Undetermined",
        "type": "Data Exposure",
        "description": "This print may seem like a security issue, but it's not. Under normal conditions all argv arguments are terminated with 0 so printf can only print the argument itself. The only issue is invoking the program via execve, but if attacker can do this, he already has full control over system and doesn't need to cause DOS.",
        "exploit": "",
        "recommendation": "Short term, \nLong term, \n"
      },
      "locations": [
